WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.433 --> 00:00:00.800
Let's bring

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:01.267
a special

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.669
guest at this White House event,

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:05.739
our own Don Lemon, who is going to appear

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:08.942
right now with his fiancee, Tim Malone.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.810
Don, you normally cover these things

00:00:10.810 --> 00:00:11.778
as a journalist here.

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:14.080
You are attending as somebody whom

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.782
this law could potentially affect.

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:16.549
Why was it important

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.218
for you to attend the signing?

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:19.652
Well, hi, Jake. How are you?

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:21.721
Thank you for having us on.

00:00:21.721 --> 00:00:23.590
Tim is now getting to understand

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:25.492
what I do is so it's hard to hear.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:26.493
We're right by the speaker

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:27.627
and we're trying to listen to you

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:28.862
and feel it.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:29.462
Well, it's

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:32.732
not likely to it will affect us.

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:35.068
And we are happy to be here

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:36.469
to witness this moment.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:37.170
It was important

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:38.271
when he got the invitation

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:39.305
from the White House.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:40.440
I said immediately,

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.841
absolutely, we want to come

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.610
and we want to experience this.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.378
As you know, Jake,

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:46.713
we got engaged just before

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:47.447
COVID happened.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.581
We're in the process

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:49.516
of planning our wedding

00:00:49.516 --> 00:00:51.017
and then it got sidetracked.

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.452
And then after we were able to

00:00:52.452 --> 00:00:54.587
go back to the courthouse and

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:57.290
start preparing our to get married again,

00:00:58.191 --> 00:00:59.559
we went to the courthouse

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:01.027
and got our marriage license.

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.729
It expires on December 18th,

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:03.530
but you have to get married

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:04.697
before December 18.

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:05.198
Oh, we got to go

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:05.799
stand in line

00:01:05.799 --> 00:01:07.133
at the courthouse in New York

00:01:07.133 --> 00:01:09.169
and do it all over again.

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:09.769
Tim.

00:01:09.769 --> 00:01:10.470
First of all, Tim,

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.938
let me tell you that the key for

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:12.772
these kinds of events

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.040
is to have two IFIs

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.109
in one in each one of your ears

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.043
to block out the sound.

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:18.878
I know I don't think that we had for IFB

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:19.345
for you guys,

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.182
but as a civilian,

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:22.615
what is it

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.850
like to watch President Biden

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.351
sign this legislation is

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.754
as part of the celebration amazing.

00:01:27.754 --> 00:01:28.888
I don't know what I expected

00:01:28.888 --> 00:01:29.522
to be here today,

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.891
but the crowd was pretty, pretty lively.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.293
I think everyone's in a really good mood

00:01:33.293 --> 00:01:34.928
and it's it's pretty exciting to be here.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.930
I'm glad we came. And it is packed.

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:37.831
I've been speaking to people.

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:38.898
Jake, you're here a lot.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:39.632
You've been here a lot.

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.067
You were a White House correspondent.

00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:42.068
I haven't seen this many people

00:01:42.068 --> 00:01:43.837
on the South Lawn in quite some time.

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:45.238
I think they said when the

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:47.373
the infrastructure bill was signed, maybe

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:49.008
but I mean, there's tons of people

00:01:49.008 --> 00:01:49.542
and it's great

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.312
because it's members of the LGBTQ

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:55.515
plus community and allies.

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:56.883
Our very own Margaret Hoover is here

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:58.618
who has fought for marriage equality

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.185
for so long.

00:01:59.185 --> 00:01:59.853
She's here as well.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:02.655
I mean, it's just it's fantastic.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.157
Everybody's happy.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:04.657
I was speaking

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:05.658
to some members of the press

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.327
and they said there's no vitriol,

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:08.828
there's nobody fighting about politics.

00:02:08.828 --> 00:02:10.363
Everyone is just happy to be here.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:11.731
It's a really good spirit, in a good mood

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.465
right now.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:13.833
The mood was

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:15.001
all smiles

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.636
and everyone was happy

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:20.039
there was very little maybe no politics

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.040
today

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:23.042
and people were just happy to be there.

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:23.743
It was.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.944
Thousands of people

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.614
crowded onto the South Lawn Wolf.

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:28.815
I'm sure you saw the pictures

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.083
and people around the world

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:31.985
watched on CNN

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:32.819
watching the president

00:02:32.819 --> 00:02:33.520
of the United States,

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.320
the vice president,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.322
the speaker of the House,

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.324
the the House, the Senate

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.392
majority leader,

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.260
all come out

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.061
and speak about the rights

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.363
for everyone to be able

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:44.797
to get married in this country.

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:46.633
Just about basic

00:02:46.633 --> 00:02:47.634
civil rights

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:48.801
that people should have that

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.803
we're that should all be granted to us

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:52.772
under the Constitution. Absolutely.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.408
I wasn't supposed to report, Wolf, today.

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.609
I was just supposed to sort of

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:58.144
go to the ceremony because I was invited

00:02:58.144 --> 00:02:59.312
and I try to take it all in.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:00.013
It was a really

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:02.582
weird experience,

00:03:02.582 --> 00:03:03.616
quite honestly, to

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:04.350
to stand there

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.585
and watch this all happening.

00:03:05.585 --> 00:03:07.053
Was kind of an out of body experience.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.288
So why was that?

00:03:08.288 --> 00:03:10.857
I was I was happy and everybody was happy

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:13.626
because growing up, I never thought that

00:03:13.626 --> 00:03:14.160
I would

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:14.627
you know,

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.963
once I realized that I was gay,

00:03:16.963 --> 00:03:17.730
I never thought that

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:18.965
I would have the opportunity

00:03:18.965 --> 00:03:21.134
or really the privilege or the honor

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:21.801
to be married.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:22.502
I thought it was something

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:23.636
that I'd have to keep a secret.

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.471
And then obviously in 20, 15

00:03:25.471 --> 00:03:26.539
that all changed.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.608
And then I met someone a year later

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:30.276
and decided

00:03:30.276 --> 00:03:32.245
that I wanted to spend my life with him.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:34.547
And as we were planning our wedding,

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.549
as you know, Wolf, you came to you

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:37.750
and your lovely wife, Lynn,

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.986
came to our engagement party

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.055
and bought us a beautiful gift.

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.723
And then it happened.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.658
And so we it got stalled.

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:48.027
And then after COVID was,

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:48.361
you know,

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:48.995
after that,

00:03:48.995 --> 00:03:50.763
some of the restrictions were lifted.

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:51.898
We went to the courthouse

00:03:51.898 --> 00:03:54.133
finally to get our marriage license

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.868
and a couple of months ago,

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.437
it expires on December 18th.

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:59.372
If we don't do it by then,

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.106
we'll have to go back

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:01.107
and go through that process.

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:02.976
Obviously, we could have done it online,

00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:04.410
but we want it to be it's

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.445
so important,

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:06.779
especially for members

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.248
of the LGBTQ community

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:09.816
who want to get married.

00:04:09.816 --> 00:04:11.084
It's really important for us

00:04:11.084 --> 00:04:12.719
to go through the process.

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:14.420
It is a legal process

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:16.189
as well as a process of love.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.257
And so we wanted to

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.691
take all of those steps

00:04:18.691 --> 00:04:20.293
and feel all of those steps.

00:04:20.293 --> 00:04:21.961
And when I got the invitation

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:23.696
from from the White House

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:24.897
to come, this week,

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.399
I didn't want when I got to the gates,

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:27.300
I said, Oh, Mr.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:28.001
Lemon, you know,

00:04:28.001 --> 00:04:28.801
someone to come get you,

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:29.636
Jamie, or someone.

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:30.370
And I said, No,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:32.238
I want to get in this line

00:04:32.238 --> 00:04:33.506
and I want to

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.308
experience it like everybody else.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.643
We waited an hour in line.

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:38.578
We talked to people, we took pictures,

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.345
we stood there

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:40.980
and someone called me over and said,

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.116
Hey, come, you know, come, go on CNN.

00:04:43.116 --> 00:04:43.650
And I did it.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.285
So this is very important

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:47.854
for members of the LGBTQ community.

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:49.322
It's not just ceremony.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.957
It's a legal right

00:04:50.957 --> 00:04:52.325
that all Americans

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:54.127
are entitled to under the Constitution.

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:55.928
Are absolutely, absolutely right.

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.263
And congratulations.

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:58.498
I'm so happy and excited

00:04:58.498 --> 00:04:59.866
that you're going to be getting married

00:04:59.866 --> 00:05:00.800
very, very soon.

